title ALES158 — Lotus's stereo_limit: the brickwall limiter carried into stereo, the ratio→∞ corner of the linked gain — both a true ceiling and an image held whole
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Third rung this turn (after ALES156 stereo_gate and ALES157 stereo_compress, both sent). The dynamics family so far: gate (linked detector, ALES156), compressor (linked gain, ALES157). The limiter (ALES49) is the family's honest floor — the brickwall on which every richer shape rests — and in stereo it is exactly the ratio→∞ corner of ALES157's linked gain, already foreshadowed by that rung's seat-at-threshold knob law. So it is the next crux and it lands cleanly on the shape already proven.
think The lovely fact this rung records: the LINKED limiter is SIMULTANEOUSLY a true brickwall AND image-preserving. Per pair, key = max(|L|,|R|); if key <= ceil both pass; else scale both by ceil/key. The peak-holding channel lands EXACTLY on ceil (key·ceil/key = ceil), the quieter channel proportionally below it — so nothing crosses the ceiling (brickwall) AND both share one gain (image held). The independent mono limiter gives only the brickwall, pinning the loud channel while leaving the quiet one untouched → image shift. So the linked form is strictly better on the image, at the honest cost of gently pulling the quiet channel down with its loud partner (what a real stereo-linked limiter does).
think StereoLimitError = ALES49's LimitError (BadCeiling, BadRange) reused whole. Overflow: |sample|*ceil <= 32767*32767 fits i64; on the scaled path ceil < key so quotient <= |sample| and <= ceil, fits i16. Caught one real edge while writing the witness: the ceiling-at-max identity law is NOT true for sample_min (-32768), because |sample_min| = 32768 > sample_max = 32767, so that pair's key exceeds the ceiling and it scales (and mono limit itself pins -32768 to -32767). Fixed the test to use in-range magnitudes (|x| <= 32767); the code handles -32768 correctly on the scaled path (pins to ceiling, no overflow). Recorded as a caught ratchet, not a red — the law is stated for in-range audio.
think Five laws witnessed GREEN: brickwall + linked-gain (left-always-peak master: no sample crosses ceil, left'=mono limit(left) {1000,-1000,500,-1000}, right scaled same fraction {250,-250,100,-750}, independent mono limit(right)={1000,-1000,100,-1000} shown to differ), image (no expand/flip, out-of-phase over-ceiling pair stays out of phase, both land on ceiling {1000,-1000,1000}), sub-ceiling (within linked ceiling identity), ceiling-at-max (identity for in-range audio), balance/atomicity/degenerate (three refusals untouched+balanced, count0 identity).
obs No custody gate reached — purely local, two bounded i16 Clips, values only, one multiply-then-divide per channel per sample, memoryless, a self-approved design round. TAME bans clean, no red (one caught test-edge on sample_min ceiling-at-max). Recorded lesson: the stereo dynamics family now has three rungs proving one arc — the gate links the DECISION, the compressor links the GAIN, and the limiter is the compressor's ratio→∞ where the linked gain becomes a brickwall that is also image-preserving (a property the independent limiter cannot claim). The downward expander (ALES60) is the natural next member — it inverts the compressor below the threshold, and its stereo law will again be a linked gain (key = max, so a quiet pair is expanded together, the image held). Front doors synced in the same commit.
loom witness=ales_stereo_limit_witness result=GREEN laws=brickwall-linked-gain+image+sub-ceiling+ceiling-at-max+balance channels=2 class=stereo-dynamics-linked-gain-ratio-infinity detector=linked-max(|L|,|R|) gain=ceil/key-shared cases=brickwall-linked(left-always-peak:no-cross,left'=mono-limit(left){1000,-1000,500,-1000},right-same-fraction{250,-250,100,-750},independent-mono-right{1000,-1000,100,-1000}-differs)+image(no-expand/flip,out-of-phase-over-ceiling-stays{1000,-1000,1000})+sub-ceiling(within-key-identity)+ceiling-at-max(in-range-identity)+balance/atomicity(3-refusals-untouched-balanced,count0-identity) caught=ceiling-at-max-not-true-for-sample_min(|.|=32768>32767)-test-fixed-to-in-range reds=0
file lotus/stereo_limit.rye ALES158 — stereo_limit, the brickwall limiter lifted to stereo as the ratio→∞ corner of ALES157's linked gain: key = max(|left|,|right|), both channels scaled by ceil/key so the peak-holder pins to ceil (brickwall) and the L:R ratio holds (image); StereoLimitError = ALES49's LimitError reused whole.
